  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool; acc 0.591), showing that multiprofile + avgpool is a strong RNA setup. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA) across all experiments, leaving the encoder choice as a major unexplored design axis. Question: Does a learned single-cell encoder (scvi_n200) outperform linear PCA in the best-performing multiprofile+avgpool configuration? This directly tests whether the encoder captures non-linear biological structure that PCA misses. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a foundational design decision that will propagate into all multimodal experiments. Resolving whether scvi or PCA is superior here (with a clean single-variable change from config_002) reduces uncertainty efficiently before committing budget to the larger multimodal grid. If scvi matches or beats PCA, it reshapes the multimodal search; if it underperforms, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can pivot to multimodal fusion with confidence."
}

